  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 134 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nMuch cooler temperatures (especially daytime highs) are forecast for \nthe start of the work week across West Central Texas. Highs on \nMonday will be a bit tricky. The current forecast indicates highs in \nthe low to mid 50s. Abundant cloud cover is forecast so it is \npossible that part of the region remain in the 40s much of the day \nMonday. For now, bumped temperatures down by a few degrees, but \ndidn't go as cold as the WOOF-NAM, but will continue to monitor. \nHighs on Tuesday will be a few degrees warmer than forecast highs on \nMonday, in the mid 50s to near 60. Highs on Wednesday will be back \ninto low to mid 60s.\n\nThursday through the end of the work week, a large upper level \ntrough is forecast to develop across the western CONUS. There \ncontinue to be differences in the strength and timing of this \nfeature between the GFS and ECMWF. For now, have kept rain chances \nfor the end of the work week in the low to medium (20-40%) range, \nbut these will likely need to eventually be adjusted. Highs Thursday \nand Friday will be in the mid 60s to lower 70s. Overnight lows will \nbe in the 50s.",
